// ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ DEMO MAIN ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓ {


if bar_index == last_bar_index - 1
	// ---  test values --- {
	b = true 	// bool
	i = 1 		// int
	f = 1. 		// float
	s = "aaa"	// string
	lnB = line.new(bar_index - 3, low[3], bar_index, low, color = color.yellow)
	lnT = line.new(time[6], low[6], time[3], low[3], color = color.rgb(255, 148, 134), xloc = xloc.bar_time)
	lblB = label.new(bar_index,high, "test", color = color.yellow)
	lblT = label.new(time[6],high[6], "test", color = color.yellow, xloc = xloc.bar_time)
	bxB =  box.new(bar_index - 3, low[3], bar_index,low, text = "box", bgcolor = color.rgb(170, 237, 246, 57))
	bxT =  box.new(time[6], low[6], time[3], low[3], text = "box", bgcolor = color.rgb(243, 213, 169, 59), xloc = xloc.bar_time)


	arB = array.from(true,false)
	arI = array.from(10,20)
	arF = array.from(30,40.)
	arS = array.from("AAA","BBB")
	arC = array.from(color.red, #00bcd4)
	arLn = array.from(lnB,lnT)
	arLbl = array.from(lblB,lblT)
	arBx = array.from(bxB,bxT)
	arT = array.from(time,time[1])

	mxF = matrix.new<float>()
	mxF.add_row(0, arI)
	mxF.add_row(0, arF)
	// mxFS = mxF.toStringMx("0.000")
	// arMxFS1 = mxFS.row(1).join(", ")
	
	// map<string, string>
	mpSS = map.new<string, string>()
	mpSS.put("aa", "AA") 
	mpSS.put("cc", string(na))
	mpSS.put("bb", "BB")

	// map<int, float>
	mpIF = map.new<int, float>()
	mpIF.put(1, 10.)
	mpIF.put(2, na)
	mpIF.put(3, -12.)
	//}

	// --- output toS() to a var --- {
	txt = ""

	
 	// ━━━━━ test arrays.toS() ━━━━━ {
	txt += "\n -------------- arrays .toS () ------------------- \n"
	txt+= "arB 		.toS()	: " +	arB 		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arI 		.toS()	: " +	arI 		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arF 		.toS()	: " +	arF 		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arC 		.toS(format = \"HEX\")	: " +	arC 		.toS(format = "HEX")		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arC 		.toS()	: " +	arC 		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= "\narS 		.toS()	: " +	arS 		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= str.format("arS.toS().length() = {0}",  	str.length(arS.toS()))		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arLn		.toS()	: " +	arLn		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arLbl	.toS()	: " +	arLbl		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arBx		.toS()	: " +	arBx		.toS()		+ "\n"
	txt+= "arT 		.toS(\"<time>\")	: " +	arT 		.toS(format = "<time>")		+ "\n"
	//}


 	// ━━━━━ test arrays.toStringAr() ━━━━━ {
	txt += "\n -------------- arrays.toStringAr () ------------------- \n"
	txt += "bool[]: toStringAr()" + arB.toStringAr().join(", ") + ", formatted: " + arB.toStringAr("<{0}>")	.join(", ")
	bool b1 = arB.get(0)
	txt += "\n ---------------------------------"				
	txt += "\n" +"b = " + b.toS() 
		  + ", arB.get(0).toS() = " + arB.get(0).toS() 
		  + ", b1 = " + b1.toS() 
	txt += "\n" + "int[]	toStringAr(): " + arI.toStringAr()												.join(", ")
	txt += "\n" + "float[]	toStringAr(): " + arF.toStringAr("0.00")										.join(", ")
	txt += "\n" + "string[]	toStringAr(): " + arS.toStringAr()												.join(", ")
	txt += "\n ---------------------------------"				
	txt += "\n" + "int[] time toStringAr(\"date\\ntime\")\n: " + arT.toStringAr("date\ntime")												.join(", ")
	txt += "\n" + "int[] time toStringAr(\"{0, date, dd} {0, time, HH:mm:ss}\"):\n " + arT.toStringAr("{0, date, dd} {0, time, HH:mm:ss}")												.join(", ")
	txt += "\n ---------------------------------"				
	txt += "\n" + "color[] toStringAr(\"HEX\"):\n " + arC.toStringAr("HEX")									.join(", ")
	txt += "\n" + "color[] toStringAr(\"RGB\"):\n " + arC.toStringAr("RGB")									.join(", ")
	txt += "\n ---------------------------------"				
	
	txt += "\n" + "line[]	toStringAr():\n" + arLn.toStringAr()												.join(",\n ")
	txt += "\n --------------------------------- "
	txt += "\n" + "line[]	toStringAr(<x1/x2>-<y1/y2>):\n" + arLn.toStringAr("<x1/x2>-<y1/y2>")				.join(",\n ")
	txt += "\n --------------------------------- "

	txt += "\n" + "label[]	toStringAr() (one label has xloc.bar_index, another - xloc.bar_time):\n" 			 + arLbl.toStringAr()								.join(",\n ")
	txt += "\n --------------------------------- "
	txt += "\n" + "label[]	toStringAr(<x1,y1>:txt) (same array another format):\n" + arLbl.toStringAr("<x1,y1>:txt") 					.join(",\n ")
	txt += "\n --------------------------------- "
	
	txt += "\n" + "box[]	toStringAr() wrapped:\n" 			 		+ arBx.toStringAr()							.join(", ") // .wrap(24, "", "> ")
	txt += "\n --------------------------------- "
	txt += "\n" + "box[]	toStringAr(<x1/x2><y1/y2>):\n" + arBx.toStringAr("<x1/x2><y1/y2>") 		.join(",\n ")
	//}
	
	//}


	// --- draw table --- {
	// TEST ALL 
	t = table.new(position.bottom_center, 2, 1, bgcolor = color.rgb(245, 243, 149), border_color = color.black, border_width = 1, frame_color = color.black, frame_width = 1)
	table.cell(t,0,0, text_halign = text.align_left,width = i_cell1W, height = 100 , text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
	table.cell(t,1,0, text_halign = text.align_left,width = i_cell2W, height = 100 , text_font_family = font.family_monospace)

	table.cell_set_text(t, 0, 0, txt)
